+The action `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` is the single entry point for calling
+the next ticket. It accepts a `Queue`, a `User`, and a `CallMode` enum
+(`Any`, `PriorityOnly`, `NormalOnly`). Ordering is: highest priority first,
+oldest `issued_at` first, lowest `id` last.
+
+**Concurrency protection** uses two `SELECT FOR UPDATE` locks (queue row, then
+candidate row) inside a database transaction. If the candidate was already
+called by a concurrent request, a `RuntimeException` is thrown.
+
+**Fairness** is checked via a query for the last 3 called tickets in the
+queue (ordered by `called_at DESC, id DESC`). If all 3 are priority and at
+least one normal ticket is waiting, `Any` mode forces normal-only selection.
+A normal call resets the streak; calls from any mode count in the history.
 
