diff --git a/docs/business-rules.md b/docs/business-rules.md
index 6f98015..66abb8d 100644
--- a/docs/business-rules.md
+++ b/docs/business-rules.md
@@ -130,6 +130,29 @@ ### Call Panel (attendant)
 
 After each call, the ticket leaves the waiting queue and enters the session/display call history.
 
+### Call implementation
+
+The domain action `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` implements the call logic and
+accepts a `App\Enums\CallMode` enum (`Any`, `PriorityOnly`, `NormalOnly`).
+
+**Locking strategy:** the action acquires a row lock on the target queue
+(`SELECT … FOR UPDATE`), selects a candidate, acquires a row lock on the
+candidate (`SELECT … FOR UPDATE`), re-checks that the candidate is still
+`waiting`, then marks it as `called` and returns the updated model. This
+prevents two concurrent attendants from calling the same ticket. An inactive
+queue is rejected (state is re-read from the database, not trusted from the
+caller).
+
+**Fairness mechanism:** in `Any` mode, if the last 3 tickets called in the
+queue are all priority and at least one normal ticket is waiting, the action
+forces normal-only selection. A normal call resets the streak. Calls from any
+mode count in the fairness history. If fairness forces normal but no normal
+ticket is waiting, priority tickets keep being called.
+
+**Mode filters:** `PriorityOnly` selects only tickets with `priority > 0`;
+`NormalOnly` selects only tickets with `priority = 0`. The fairness rule
+overrides mode filters only in `Any` mode when the fairness condition is met.
+
